  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">China-Ghana Engagement and Strategic Partnership Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Four main interrelated approaches will be adopted to drive and deliver this project to achieve outlined outcomes. These mutually reinforcing approaches, all collaborative, are awareness raising; engagement of key stakeholders (including the Chinese Embassy, Chinese Chamber of Commerce, Ministry of Trade and Industry, Ghana Union of Traders Association, labour unions); research; and co -creation and design of activities and programmes. As part of this set of approaches a mix of tools and methods, including statements and media outreach, closed door Chatham House rules meetings, mobilisation, lobbying with policy makers (both Chinese and Ghanaian officials) and private sector and networking, and coalition -building will be adopted as and when necessary.</narrative>
  </description>
